<H1 align="center">A review of the ODE solvers of Axiom, Derive, Macsyma, Maple, Mathematica,
    MuPAD and Reduce
</H1>

<h3 align="center">
<A HREF="../../participants.html#Postel">Frank Postel</A>,
<A HREF="../../participants.html#Zimmermann">Paul Zimmermann</A><br>
</h3>

Date: July 20th (Saturday) <br>
Time: 9:37.5<br>

<center>
Abstract
</center>

Using a wide set of more than 50 different kinds of ordinary differential equations
    and systems, we try to give an idea of the capabilities of Axiom, Derive, Macsyma, Maple,
    Mathematica, MuPAD and Reduce in solving differential equations. In our conclusion we
    firstly want to give the user an answer to the question "What system should I use?" and
    secondly to point out to developers of computer algebra systems the advantages and/or
    drawbacks of their ODE solver, to help to improve it. 

